// What `<<|` yields for the keys that are not letters.
//
// BUG-ZYB-006: Ctrl+A used to arrive as the letter `a`, Ctrl+C as `c`, and Tab
// and Backspace as the same NUL — so a full-screen program could not offer a
// single Ctrl shortcut (one would fire when the user typed that letter into a
// text field) and could not tell Tab from Backspace (in a form, every jump
// between fields would erase a character).
//
// This case needs a GOLDEN and not just engine agreement: both engines were
// wrong in the same way, and a suite that only asks whether they agree cannot
// see that. It is the same split zyquality draws everywhere — the goldens are
// the gate, the consensus is a finding.
>>| {
    @ _i:1..8 {
        <<| t
        >> ##!t " "
    }
}
